      "writtenOn": "2024-12-11T14:46:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ptdump does not care about the hardware address. So how about we compress things a bit here with addr? I know it\u0027d be a bit more cumbersome, but then the whole page-table description is more likely to hold on a single page.\n\n```\nstruct pkvm_ptdump_log {\n    u64 addr: 52;\n    bool valid: 1;\n    bool r: 1;\n    bool w: 1;\n    bool xn: 1;\n    /* I don\u0027t believe we use AF */\n    bool blk: 1;\n    enum pkvm_page_state: 2;\n    s8 level;\n};\n```\n\nThis would save 64-bits per buffer entry.\n\nAlso as we know ptdump is a slow operation, we could __packed to save few more bits.\n\nIt would mean though we have to \"deserialize\" it into an original PTE to reuse \"note_page()\"",
      "revId": "e638429db575ac0d4f87f0d61a092859d9812081",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
